Poisson bracket preservation on all generators: VERIFIED (all canonical relations hold)
Non-invertibility: on the section p = 0, Psi(q, 0) = (F(q), 0); the
three verified collision points give Psi(a,0) = Psi(b,0) = Psi(c,0)
with a,b,c distinct => Psi is not injective on points => not a
polynomial automorphism => NOT a Poisson automorphism.
=> THE POISSON CONJECTURE (PC_3 on C^6, hence stably) IS FALSE,
   with the explicit witness Psi = (F, (JF^T)^{-1} p).
